{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1352341-exigent-charms-for-ten-sheaves","id":1352341,"title":"Exigent charms for Ten Sheaves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-03T05:33:10-08:00","id":1352341,"title":"Exigent charms for Ten Sheaves","content":"In the main 3e Exalted book, it describes a particular Exigent, Janest, chosen by Ten Sheaves. I designed some homebrew charms for her in advance of her possibly getting official charms in the Exigent book:<br /> <b>Grain-Measuring Stick</b> (3m; Reflexive; Instant) Janest measures the opponent\u2019s attack as she would a stalk of grain, and finds it wanting. This charm is activated when Janest is attacked, before the attack is rolled. Choose a number form 1 to 5 (or below the target number of the attack if that attack has an unusual target number), and then subtract a number of successes from the attack equal to the number of times this number is rolled.<br /> <br /> <b>Reaping and Sowing </b>(10m; Reflexive; Scene) For the rest of the scene, whenever Janest kills a Fair Folk or other creature of the Wyld, she heals a number of health levels equal to their Essence. This starts with Bashing, and cannot heal aggravated health levels. Lowering a battlegroup\u2019s Size heals the Essence of one member of the battlegroup.<br /> <br /> <b>Inviolable Skyscraper Stalk </b>(3m, 1wp; Simple; Scene) The strength of Janest\u2019s spirit would let a single stalk of wheat stand with the tallest towers of Wu-Jian. None will force her from her place. For the rest of the scene, she gains several benefits: She gets a +4 bonus to resist attempts to move her or knock her down (or +2 to static values). She may attack flying enemies with melee attacks as long as the horizontal part of their distance is within close range. She ignores onslaught penalties to her defense. She loses 1 less initiative than normal from withering attacks, though the attacker still gains initiative as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Sublime Homeomorphism Invariance </b>(2m; Supplemental; Instant) Janest is so attuned to the land that difference along it means nothing to her. She disappears into the tall grass and reappears somewhere else, to defend her home against any number of invaders. This Charm supplements Ten Sheaves\u2019 movement for her turn. She can move up two two range bands, and does not need to roll disengage, as long as she moves into a space with an enemy and as long as the area she moves through is field, grass, scrubland, or similar environments.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohomology</b> <b>Revelation Strike</b> (6m; Supplemental) Janest cuts through an enemy\u2019s physical form to reveal their true essence. Their base defense is cut in half, rounded down. This does not affect bonuses to defense from excellencies, willpower, charms, or magic, or stunts, but does affect full defense and mounted bonuses. On a Withering attack, this charm also removes Soak equal to the number of extra successes on the attack roll (but cannot remove Soak from Stamina). On a Decisive attack, this charm also grants double 10s on damage rolls.<br /> <br /> These charms are designed to fit with various aspects of her story (her god, her appearance, what her god asks her to do) as well as to fit a somewhat obscure pun. I hope there is someone on here who finds them as funny as I do, and can maybe even add additional ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T06:54:37-08:00","id":1352353,"title":"","content":"Wow, the pun is... Heavy. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I imagine that the cohomology charm should be designed along the lines &quot;upon making three move actions, if you manage to return to your initial position with the enemy encircled with your path, your health levels, willpower and motes are all one hogher than at the initial point of the path.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: you're definitely missing a germ-themed charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 12-03-2019, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T08:16:24-08:00","id":1352366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1352341-exigent-charms-for-ten-sheaves?p=1352353#post1352353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, the pun is... Heavy. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I imagine that the cohomology charm should be designed along the lines &quot;upon making three move actions, if you manage to return to your initial position with the enemy encircled with your path, your health levels, willpower and motes are all one hogher than at the initial point of the path.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: you're definitely missing a germ-themed charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to do a more abstract interpretation of cohomology with a &quot;reveal their true essence&quot;, which I think is a fair description of what cohomology does in many different contexts. Did you catch the mechanical reference to her book story in that charm? But she could also have the charm you suggested - maybe one is the prerequisite of the other.<br /> <br /> Germ is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}